  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For the plane electromagnetic wave given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;the&nbsp;ratio of average electric energy density to average magnetic energy density is&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
  },
